Keep status delays independent of logging

The systemd daemon enables info logs for connection diagnostics. Using
that setting to bypass SlowGuard's delay makes short CLI operations
print status messages immediately. Preserve the ten-second initial
delay regardless of logging verbosity.

Add an integration test that enables daemon info logging and briefly
blocks a real listing request, then checks that the CLI succeeds with
empty stderr. This covers the daemon-to-client status path shared by
pod listing and the pod creation checks used during agent startup.
